The following upstream designs were studied as concept-level references for
original AgentOS-uCore implementations:

- Linux CPU accounting and batched per-CPU/rstat accounting ideas:
  https://docs.kernel.org/6.11/admin-guide/cgroup-v1/cpuacct.html
  https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/lib/percpu_counter.c
  https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/kernel/cgroup/rstat.c
- Linux BPF ring buffer ordering, reserve/commit/discard, and notification
  ideas: https://docs.kernel.org/6.6/bpf/ringbuf.html
- Haiku BFS attributes, selective indexing, and live-query ideas:
  https://www.haiku-os.org/legacy-docs/practical-file-system-design.pdf
- Linux cgroup v2, blk-mq, and wait-queue documentation:
  https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.html
  https://docs.kernel.org/block/blk-mq.html
  https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/kernel/sched/wait.c
- Linux EEVDF scheduling concepts, including lag eligibility, virtual
  deadlines, and sleeping-lag decay:
  https://docs.kernel.org/scheduler/sched-eevdf.html
- io_uring's submission-queue/completion-queue communication model:
  https://kernel.dk/io_uring.pdf
- WebAssembly Component Model WIT resource ownership and WASI 0.3 async,
  future, and stream interface concepts:
  https://component-model.bytecodealliance.org/design/wit.html
  https://component-model.bytecodealliance.org/design/async.html
- AgentCgroup's published measurements of tool-call-level Agent resource
  bursts (arXiv:2602.09345):
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.09345
- Murakkab's declarative workflow and execution-configuration/SLO separation
  (arXiv:2508.18298):
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.18298
- CaMeL's trusted-control-flow/untrusted-data-flow security architecture
  (arXiv:2503.18813):
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.18813
- IPIGuard's planned Tool Dependency Graph security model
  (arXiv:2508.15310):
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.15310
- Model Context Protocol 2026-07-28 and its draft Tasks extension, used as
  user-space gateway protocol references:
  https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28
  https://tasks.extensions.modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft/tasks
- Agent2Agent Protocol v1 Task, Context, Artifact, streaming, and cancellation
  objects, used as user-space gateway protocol references:
  https://a2a-protocol.org/latest/whats-new-v1/
  https://a2a-protocol.org/latest/specification/
- AIOS paper and repository, used only as public project/evaluation references:
  https://openreview.net/attachment?id=L4HHkCDz2x&name=pdf
  https://github.com/agiresearch/AIOS

These references are not vendored dependencies. The Workflow Credit Domain,
Tool Phase Credit Lease, workflow-level EEVDF, declarative Execution Contract,
Context Provenance enforcement, typed Agent Task Channel, MCP/A2A user-space
gateway, Fence-Sealed Evidence Ring, and Agent Live-Query FS were implemented
in this repository as clean-room, project-specific code after studying public
design principles and protocol documents. No Linux, Haiku, AIOS, paper-prototype,
MCP/A2A SDK, or WebAssembly/WASI source code, test data, binaries, generated
artifacts, or on-disk formats are copied or redistributed by those mechanisms.
Names such as cgroup, percpu_counter, rstat, BPF ring buffer, BFS, live query,
EEVDF, SQ/CQ, WIT, WASI, MCP, and A2A identify conceptual or protocol lineage,
not source or binary compatibility. AgentOS-uCore does not embed io_uring, a
WebAssembly runtime, or an in-kernel MCP/A2A networking stack.
